WEBVTT

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.400
All right.
Let's review this one more time.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.880
At precisely 8:32-ish,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.040
Exhibit A, Woody, was kidnapped.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.480
Exhibit B,
a composite sketch of the kidnapper.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.600
-He didn't have a beard like that.
-Fine. Etch, give him a shave.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.720
SLINKY: The kidnapper
was bigger than that.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.880
-Oh, picky, picky, picky.
-Let's just go straight to Exhibit F.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.640
The kidnapper's vehicle.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.520
Now, the vehicle fled the scene
in this direction.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.800
Your eyes are in backwards.
It went the other way.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.920
Hey. Put a cork in it.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.280
-How do you spell FBI?
-My crime scene!

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.480
Oh, why don't you watch
where you're going, Godspilla?

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.240
-I didn't know there was a crime scene.
-Excuse me. Excuse me.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.560
-A little quiet, please. Thank you.
-Huh?

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.400
MR. SPELL: Lazy toy brain.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.600
-Lousy try, Brian.
-What are you doing, Buzz?

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.640
It's some sort of message
encoded on that vehicle's I.D. tag.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.960
-Liz try bran.
-It's just a license plate.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.800
-It's just a jumble of letters.
-Yeah, and there are about

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.720
3.5 million registered cars
in the tri-county area alone.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.640
-Lou's thigh burn.
-(BUZZ GROANING)

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.560
Oh, this can't help.
Let's leave Buzz to play with his toys.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.880
Toy. Toy. Toy. Hold on!

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.520
(MR. SPELL BEEPING
ELECTRONICALLY)

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.720
-Al's Toy Barn.
-Al's Toy Barn!

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.880
Etch, draw that man in a chicken suit.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.800
-(ALL GASPING)
-It's the chicken man!

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.440
BUZZ: That's our guy.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.600
I knew there was something
I didn't like about that chicken.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.640
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'll be right there.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.080
And we're gonna do this commercial
in one take, do you hear me,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.040
because I am in the middle
of something really important.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.880
-(PHONE BEEPS OFF)
-(CHUCKLING MANIACALLY)

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.840
You, my little cowboy friend,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.600
are gonna make me
big buck, buck, bucks.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.560
(GASPING, STRAINING)

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.040
(GRUNTS)

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.920
(GASPING, GRUNTING)

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.360
-(SIREN BLARING)
-(GASPS)

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.000
Andy!

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.920
I can't believe I have to drive
all the way to work on a Saturday.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.320
All the way to work!

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.640
(HORNS HONKING)

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.840
(GRUNTING)

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.480
What? Whoa!

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.360
(SCREAMING)

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.640
Hey! Stop! Horsey, stop! Stop! Sit, boy!

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.720
Stop it!
(SCREAMS) Sit, I said!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.680
Whoa! Whoa. (GRUNTS)

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.080
-Yee-haw!
-(CRIES OUT)

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.320
It's you! It's you!
It's you! It's you! It's you!

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.040
-It's really you!
-What's me?

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.200
Whoo-whee!

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.920
VOICE BOX:
There's a snake in my boot.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.400
-Ha! It is you!
-Please stop saying that.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.000
Prospector said someday you'd come.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.960
Sweet mother of Abraham Lincoln!

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.520
The Prospector!
He'll wanna meet ya! (WHISTLES)

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.440
Say "hello" to the Prospector!

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.600
-It... It's a box.
-He's mint in the box.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.520
Never been opened.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.520
PETE: Turn me around, Bullseye,
so I can see.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.320
Why, the prodigal son has returned.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.360
Yee-haw!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.680
It's you! It's you!

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.480
You're here!
It's you! It's you! It's you!

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.960
Okay. I'm officially freaked out now.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:19.040
Oh, we've waited countless years
for this day.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.640
-It's good to see you, Woody.
-Listen. I don't know...

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.480
-Hey, how do you know my name?
-Everyone knows your name, Wood-y.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:33.440
Why, you don't know
who you are, do you? Bullseye?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:42.760
(GASPS)

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.920
That's me.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.600
(GASPING)

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.600
Wow.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.120
Holy cow.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.720
(WESTERN-STYLE THEME SONG
PLAYS)

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.520
ANNOUNCER: Cowboy Crunchies,

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.120
the cereal that's sugar-frosted
and dipped in chocolate,

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.640
proudly presents...

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.720
♪ Woody's Roundup
Come on, it's time to play

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.480
♪ There's Jessie
the yodeling cowgirl

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.760
♪ Yodel-ay-hee-hoo

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.520
-(CHORUS YODELING)
-Look it! That's me!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.040
♪ Bullseye, he's Woody's horse

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:46.680
♪ He's a smart one

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.720
♪ Pete the old Prospector

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.200
Has anyone seen my pick?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.640
♪ And the man himself
Of course, it's time for Sheriff Woody

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.000
♪ He's the very best

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.280
♪ He's the rootin'-est
tootin'-est cowboy

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.240
♪ In the wild, wild west

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.800
♪ Woody's Roundup ♪

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.200
I can't find it! It doesn't seem
to be on any of these stations.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.920
-Keep looking.
-You're going too slow.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.640
Let me take the wheel.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.720
-(JUMBLED AUDIO)
-REX: It's too fast.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.320
-How can you even tell what's on?
-I can tell.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.360
-(AL SQUAWKS)
-ALL: Stop! Back, back, back!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.400
Too late. I'm in the 40s.
Got to go 'round the horn. It's faster.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.280
-ALL: Back, back! Stop!
-And look for the giant chicken!

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.360
Now, Etch!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.240
That's where I need to go.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.760
You can't go, Buzz.
You'll never make it there.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.160
Woody once risked his life to save me.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.560
I couldn't call myself his friend
if I weren't willing to do the same.

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.200
So who's with me?

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:50.960
I'm packing you an extra pair of shoes
and your angry eyes just in case.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.800
This is for Woody when you find him.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:06:59.800
(CLEARS THROAT) All right,

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.360
but I don't think it'll mean
the same coming from me.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:07.400
Mr. Buzz Lightyear,
you just gotta save my pal Woody.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.520
-(COUGHING, WHEEZING)
-I'll do my best, son.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.600
Okay, fellas. Let's roll.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.200
Geronimo!

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.200
You'd think with
all my video game experience,

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.320
I'd be feeling more prepared.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.760
(SCREAMING)

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.400
The idea is to let go.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.400
We'll be back before Andy gets home.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.800
Don't talk to any toy you don't know!

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.880
To Al's Toy Barn and beyond!

